
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIX 4 (default on, NEUTRON_D2D_LAZYTESS=0 disables): triangulate a path on first FILL,
# not in ID2D1GeometrySink::Close.
#
# Close resolved self-intersections and triangulated immediately. That output is consumed in
# exactly ONE place -- the fill path (d2d_device_context_fill_geometry); FillContainsPoint,
# ComputeArea and the stroke path all work from the figures, and the stroke OUTLINE is built
# during streaming in EndFigure. So every geometry used only as a layer mask, only stroked, or
# created and discarded paid for triangulation nobody read.
#
# Not academic: d2d_geometry_intersect_self() is O(n^2) in segments. Measured 2026-07-27 while
# zooming Premiere's timeline -- 386 Close calls on 1k-4k vertex paths at ~3.9ms EACH, plus
# 76,000 smaller ones, with CreateGeometryGroup (which builds a path and closes it internally)
# the single most frequent call at 58,000 per session.
#
#   Controlled A/B, alternating the optimisation on ALTERNATE FRAMES within one session so
#   both variants see identical work (comparing separate sessions is meaningless here -- the
#   cost depends entirely on how far the timeline is zoomed):
#       timeline frame  ON 10,907us | OFF 16,906us   (35% faster)
#       timeline frame  ON 19,355us | OFF 29,176us   (34% faster)
#       timeline frame  ON 16,340us | OFF 23,510us   (30% faster)
#
# Two traps, both hit and both fixed:
#   * A geometry GROUP takes a BY-VALUE copy of its inner path's tessellation in
#     d2d_geometry_group_init. Deferring without handling that copies empty arrays and the
#     group draws NOTHING -- every group-drawn UI element (track-header buttons, the tools
#     panel) vanished. The group now copies the outline immediately (already valid) and
#     resolves its fill through the same lazy path.
#   * Claiming must be PER GEOMETRY (interlocked compare-exchange), not behind one shared
#     lock. A process-wide critical section serialised every thread triggering a deferred
#     tessellation; Premiere runs 404 threads with a five-thread render pool, and a CEP panel
#     loading visibly queued behind it. Removing the shared lock also improved throughput
#     (26-27% -> 30-35%).
#
# ALSO REJECTED, recorded so it is not retried: adding a bounding-box rejection to
# d2d_geometry_intersect_line_line before the intersection math. MEASURED 19-20% SLOWER on
# 1k-4k vertex paths (same alternating A/B). The segments in Adobe's paths do overlap in
# bounds, so the test never paid for itself. A comment in geometry.c records this.

diff --git a/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c b/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
index c6ab60c1bc4..3392c5627ed 100644
--- a/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/bitmap.c
